From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:50:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Number each compute queue's target
 stamps on its own

With g16_compute_queues=2 every compute command took its ordinal from
one engine-wide counter, so the target stamp each firmware compute
queue saw skipped every value the other queue had taken. The firmware
requires the commands of one queue to advance its entry by exactly one
and stopped within seconds of mixed compute work:

  DAG: Non Sequential Stamp Updates seen entryIdx 0x45 roots.dag 0x44
  stampIdx 0x10 stampValue 0x4500

Give compute queues 1 to 3 their own last ordinal next to queue 0's,
which stays the engine ordinal. Everything the prefix derives from the
ordinal (the work block's target stamp, command index and id, the
queue's published tail, and the retirement and event matches against
that queue's stamp) now counts the commands of its own queue, so each
queue's stamp steps by 0x100 per command of that queue.

The last complete receipt that a late recovery snapshot is matched
against is kept per compute queue as well, since equal targets on two
queues no longer name the same command.

With one compute queue, the default, every command is on queue 0 and
the ordinals, targets and receipts are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
